{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-tsx","path":"/blog/2023-04-02--cposc-2023/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"disqus":"edward-j-schwartz"}},"post":{"html":"<p>My family and I had quite the day attending the <a href=\"https://www.cposc.org\">2023 Central Pennsylvania Open\nSource Conference (CPOSC)</a> yesterday at the Ware Center in Lancaster, PA.  In addition to attending, we spoke in three different talks!</p>\n<p>My wife, Dr. Stephanie Schwartz, kicked things off.  <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 690px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.14450867052024%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Stephanie presenting\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/15ec7/steph.jpg\"\n        srcset=\"/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/9ac50/steph.jpg 173w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/8d48c/steph.jpg 345w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/15ec7/steph.jpg 690w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/af659/steph.jpg 1035w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/89b2d/steph.jpg 1380w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/e1596/steph.jpg 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 690px) 100vw, 690px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n    </span>  She gave a\nshort introduction on Random Forests as an introduction for her student Samantha\nNoggle, in \"Machine Learning Techniques to Improve Users' Music Listening\nExperiences\".  I thought Samantha did a great job on her presentation.  It was\nan interesting topic that she presented at just the right level of detail.</p>\n<p>Next, my step son Nick Elzer, along with his coworker from\n<a href=\"https://www.quub.space\">Quub</a>, Nathaniel Every, gave his first ever public\nconference presentation, and did a great job!  <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 690px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.14450867052024%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Nick and Nathaniel\npresenting\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/15ec7/nick.jpg\"\n        srcset=\"/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/9ac50/nick.jpg 173w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/8d48c/nick.jpg 345w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/15ec7/nick.jpg 690w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/af659/nick.jpg 1035w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/89b2d/nick.jpg 1380w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/e1596/nick.jpg 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 690px) 100vw, 690px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n    </span>  Their presentation was \"SpaceHeX Beta1.0 Release - What\nIf, For Space Hardware Development, We Put Each Egg In Its Own Basket?\", and was\nabout SpaceHex, a prototyping system they open sourced to make it easier for\npeople to break into satellite development.  They also demoed a pretty sweet\nomnidirectional rover that they built (at 2am the night before, naturally).</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet\"><p lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Started the open source repo for our space hardware development platform <a href=\"https://t.co/cRzHZkM6Gg\">https://t.co/cRzHZkM6Gg</a><br><br>Had a blast presenting with <a href=\"https://twitter.com/Nick_elzer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@Nick_elzer</a> for <a href=\"https://twitter.com/quubspace?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@quubspace</a>!<br><br>Thank you <a href=\"https://twitter.com/CPOSC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@CPOSC</a> for having us! <a href=\"https://t.co/eRoHm5ea2u\">pic.twitter.com/eRoHm5ea2u</a></p>&mdash; Nathaniel Evry (@NathanielEvry) <a href=\"https://twitter.com/NathanielEvry/status/1642204542921064452?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">April 1, 2023</a></blockquote> <script async src=\"https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js\" charset=\"utf-8\"></script>\n<p>Finally, I gave a tutorial presentation called \"Introduction to Exploiting Stack\nBuffer Overflow Vulnerabilities\".  If you want, you can follow along\n<a href=\"https://github.com/edmcman/cposc-exploit\">here</a>. <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 690px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.14450867052024%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Me speaking\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/15ec7/ed.jpg\"\n        srcset=\"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/9ac50/ed.jpg 173w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/8d48c/ed.jpg 345w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/15ec7/ed.jpg 690w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/af659/ed.jpg 1035w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/89b2d/ed.jpg 1380w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/e1596/ed.jpg 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 690px) 100vw, 690px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n    </span>  In\ntheory, there are supposed to be videos of all three talks eventually.  I'll\npost them when they are made available.</p>\n<p>After a few years of hiatus, it was great to have CPOSC 2023 be back in person\nagain.  I saw a number of great presentations, and met a lot of interesting and\nsmart people.  It's always surprising how many technical people work in an area\nthat is known for its rural farming!</p>","excerpt":"My family and I had quite the day attending the 2023 Central Pennsylvania Open\nSource Conference (CPOSC) yesterday at the Ware Center in…","timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2023-04-02--cposc-2023/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["talks"],"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","twitter":"@edmcman","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png 80w","sizes":"80px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/1deab/ed.webp 80w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"80px"}]},"width":80,"height":80}}}},"title":"CPOSC 2023","updatedDate":"Apr 2, 2023","image":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/d5441/ed.jpg","srcSet":"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/d5441/ed.jpg 700w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/284f1/ed.jpg 1400w","sizes":"700px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/efd8f/ed.webp 700w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/93de6/ed.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"700px"}]},"width":700,"height":300}}}}},"recents":{"edges":[{"nod